WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.560
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:03.660
RAJ CHETTY: The American
dream is fading.

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:08.310
Only half of kids today will go on
to earn more than their parents did.

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:09.780
Why has this happened?

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:13.540
And how can we reverse the
fading of the American dream?

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:16.030
When thinking about how
to answer these questions,

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:18.960
you might not think of big
data as a place to look.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:22.290
Big data is often
associated with corporations

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:25.500
seeking to improve the products
they offer by collecting

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.900
troves of data on their customers.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.870
But what if we could use
big data for social good,

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:34.740
to address problems such as the
fading American dream, growing income

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:38.410
inequality, or persistent
racial disparities?

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:41.370
This course will teach you
how to use big data, coupled

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:43.710
with the tools of data
science and economics,

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:47.325
to solve some of the most important
social problems of our time.

00:01:10.532 --> 00:01:12.740
So the tools that you're
going to learn in this class

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:15.380
will be applicable not just
to the types of problems

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:19.190
that we'll discuss here in the United
States, but globally around the world.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:33.330
Big data helps us cut through
politically charged debates

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:38.080
and find out what policies actually
work from a scientific perspective,

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:43.470
making the often discussed notion of
evidence-based policy making a reality.

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:46.560
Big social problems
require big data solutions.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:49.610
[MUSIC PLAYING]

